PHOTO_TAGGING_PROMPT = '''You are tagging real estate listing photos so a marketer can pick the best ones for social posts. Reply with ONE line only, no quotes, no line breaks, in exactly this shape: ROOM: <one of front exterior, rear exterior, aerial, street view, kitchen, living room, dining room, primary bedroom, other bedroom, bathroom, laundry, garage, office, backyard, pool, view, detail, floor plan, other> | SOCIAL: <1 to 10, how strong this is as a standalone social post: light, sharpness, composition, uncluttered> | SHAPE: <landscape or portrait or square> | SEE: <at most 10 words naming the visible features, only what you can actually see> | STORY: <the single most distinctive thing about THIS photo that a storyteller would point out, 12 to 30 words. Look for: a material or finish (stone, tile, wood, metal), an architectural detail (vaulted ceiling, beams, arch, fireplace, built-ins), how two spaces connect, a sightline through a window or door, the setting around the home, or an object that gives the room its character. Name the actual thing. Mention light or shadows only if that is truly the standout, and never guess the time of day. Only what you can actually see, with no opinions and no guesses about the neighborhood or the people> | POST: <yes or no. Answer no if ANY of these is true: the main subject is a bathroom, toilet, shower, laundry, closet, garage interior, utility area, hallway, floor plan or storage; a person, a pet, a car license plate or personal items such as framed family photos are clearly visible; the photo is dark, blurry, tilted or cluttered; the yard or ground is bare, dirty, weedy or unfinished and is the main subject; a mess or damage is visible; an old, weathered, leaning, rundown or derelict barn, shed or outbuilding is the main subject. Otherwise answer yes> | WHY: <at most 8 words giving the reason when POST is no, otherwise the word ok> | FEATURE: <none, or the single most marketable feature clearly visible, chosen from: pool, spa or hot tub, large shop or barn in good condition, waterfront or lake or river or pond, outdoor kitchen or covered patio, mountain or valley or water view, large open lot, guest house, orchard or vineyard, other. Count a feature only if it is substantial and clearly visible: a small creek, a puddle, a drainage ditch, or a lake too far away to really make out does NOT count as water. An old, weathered, leaning or rundown barn, shed or outbuilding does NOT count> | SCALE: <at most 10 words on how big and substantial that feature really looks in this photo, or none>'''



